Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10 56 CLINICAL DATA  Locally advanced breast cancer status post CA taxol  developed tumor while pregnant                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE  1  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  Multiple small nodules dispersed within at least a 5cm area  Grade  3  Lymphatic vessel invasion  Present  extensive  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Location of ductal carcinoma in situ  Within and beyond the region of the mass  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   NODE DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 9 LYMPH NODES  SEE TABLE  2  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES Number of positive lymph nodes  2  Number of lymph nodes examined  9  Number of lymph nodes with metastases less than 0 2cm  1  Size of largest lymph node  0 8cm metastatic deposit in a 1 5cm lymph node  Extracapsular extension  None  Other forms of axillary involvement  None  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 18 04                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 17 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axillary tail and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm intact skin ellipse  The specimen is oriented with a stitch designating 12 o clock  The excised margin is inked black and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm hard  ill defined  stellate  tan to tan pink mass  which comes to 2 0cm from the closest posterior margin  4 5cm from the closest superior margin  7 0cm from the inferior margin  1 2cm from the closest anterior margin  skin   and is located 5 0cm lateral to the nipple  Also identified is an accentuation of the parenchyma  which comes to 0 5cm from the closest posterior margin and 1 0cm from the closest inferior margin  Section Code  A G  Representative sections of the tumor  the tumor related to the skin is in A and C  the posterior margin in E and F   H  A representative section of parenchyma  I  Breast parenchyma related to the anterior inferior margin  J  Breast parenchyma related to the posterior margin  K  Breast parenchyma related to the inferior margin  Dissection of the axillary tail shows 9 lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE The lymph nodes are entirely submitted in cassette L O  Resident  Mari Mino  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  