 compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of breast with an indistinct firm area and a localizing wire in place   No accompanying radiograph   Sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular tan firm lesion  extending to within 0 5cm of surface ink  There is adjacent parenchymal hemorrhage  Sections of mass in A through D  with other representative sections in E through J  Received labeled  left axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of fatty tissue containing multiple tan rubbery lymph node as large as 1 1cm  submitted in cassettes K through N  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST EXCISION PART B  LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES   report_end  , 0.
