Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  09 AUG 94 at 13 16 CLINICAL DATA  38 year old female with cancer of left breast  Status post chemotherapy with regression of tumor  now for mastectomy  Please do receptors on any residual tumor                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  WIDESPREAD  WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVASION  REMOVED_DATE LYMPH NODES ARE INVOLVED BY MICROSCOPIC FOCI OF CARCINOMA SURGICAL MARGINS NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE  LEFT BREAST   METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA WITHIN LYMPHATICS AND ONE LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  James F  Southern  M D  Signed On  24 AUG 94 at 14 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast   is a 670 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm overlying skin ellipse containing an unremarkable nipple and a 3 0cm long circum areolar healed surgical incision 2 0cm inferomedial to the nipple  The resection margins are inked and the specimen is serially sectioned from the posterior surface to reveal a hard  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm  irregular  white  fibrotic area with a central yellowish region identified directly deep to the circum areolar healed incision  this is presumed to be the biopsy cavity and it is 1 5cm from the deep margin  The rest of the breast parenchyma shows multiple ill defined areas of tan white  fibrotic tissue scattered throughout the breast  The axillary tail is separated from the main mass and sampled for lymph nodes  which measure in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in aggregate  SECTION CODE  A  nipple  B  healed incision  C D  presumed biopsy cavity  E  deep margin  F H  representative sections of breast tissue  I J  representative sections of suspicious area adjacent to axillary tail  K  lymph nodes  Labeled  Left breast  additional axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of yellow tan  soft tissue  submitted entirely in L  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  F